# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Move the single card offered by a Scry 1 GroupReq from the top to the bottom of the library.
# Forcing: Wall of Runes is the only spell, one Island pays for it, and the known top two cards make the result observable.
# AI behavior: The opponent has no hand or meaningful choice while the enter-the-battlefield ability resolves.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN   = Wall of Runes resolves and Grizzly Bears moves beneath the Forests.
#   LOSE  = the spell or scry result fails and the known library order is unchanged.
#   TIMEOUT = the GroupReq or its response fails to advance.
# Card roles:
#   Wall of Runes — creates the Scry 1 interaction.
#   Grizzly Bears — the known top card selected for the library bottom.
#   Forest — makes the post-scry library top deterministic.
# Protocol path: cast and resolution messages followed by GroupReq and GroupResp.

[metadata]
